IMPORT prelude

-- Central Provident Fund (Self-Employed Persons) Regulations 1992 (Rg 25), made under s 77(1) of the Central Provident Fund Act
-- 1953 -- the figures that s 9A leaves to regulations: who is a "self-employed person" (reg 2(1)), the exclusion of platform
-- remuneration (reg 2A, the s 8A(9) date), the $6,000 threshold (reg 3), the amount (reg 4(1)(m) and First Schedule item 23),
-- rounding (reg 14), the deduction of estimated contributions (reg 8A), the time and manner of payment (reg 7A), additional
-- contributions (regs 8 and 13), and the application to reduce contributions to the Third Schedule maximum (reg 9A).
--
-- Edition: informal consolidation, version in force from 1 January 2026 (current as at 13 October 2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953-RG25.txt (SSO PDF dated 30 December 2025). Regs 2A, 3(2), 7A(4A), 9, 9A and the Third
-- Schedule as amended by S 888/2025 wef 1 January 2026. The Act's s 2(1A)(a) (when an age is attained) is read from
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CPFA1953.txt.
--
-- WHY. Added on 12 October 2026 for REQ-0268 (Haziq scenario, event from the Jun Hao scenario, event j043, 2028): "A self-employed
-- delivery rider declares $31,000 of trade income for a year. What Medisave contribution must he make, and by when?" The sibling
-- module cpf-self-employed.l4 encodes the Act's s 9A with a labelled stand-in rate; this module supplies the regulations' figures
-- and the case file uses it. cpf-self-employed.l4 is not changed beyond a pointer.
--
-- THE FIRST SCHEDULE TABLE in the .txt deposit is laid out column by column across two pages. Item 23 was read cell by cell and
-- checked for continuity: every age column joins up at $12,000 and $18,000 (e.g. 4% x 12,000 = 480 = the $480 base; 480 + 0.16 x
-- 6,000 = 1,440 = 8% x 18,000), and every cap is the top rate on $96,000. So the reading is internally consistent.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: items 1 to 22 of the First Schedule (relevant years before 2026); Members of Parliament (regs 3(2), 5, 10 and the
-- Second Schedule); relevant public officers (reg 4(2), 6% or the Minister for Health's figure); regs 4(3)-(11), 6, 7 and 15 (years
-- before 2023 or before 2020); reg 9 (years before 2025); recomputation by the Board (reg 7A(5)) beyond taking the recomputed figure
-- as an input; voluntary contributions (regs 17, 17AB); moneys applied from nominations or grants (reg 17A); registration, returns,
-- service and addresses (regs 18-24); the Minister's exemption (reg 25); the s 9(2) interest rate, which this instrument does NOT
-- prescribe; and where the money is credited (s 13(4) and the Minister's direction; this instrument does not say "medisave" for
-- reg 4 contributions).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent
-- test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Central Provident Fund (Self-Employed Persons) Regulations 1992`

§§ `Regs 2, 2A, 3 -- to whom the Regulations apply`

-- Reg 2(1): "'self-employed person' means any person, being a citizen or permanent resident of Singapore, who accrues, derives or
-- receives income, and includes a Member of Parliament." "'income' means the assessable income accrued in or derived from Singapore
-- or received in Singapore from outside Singapore from any trade, business, profession or vocation other than from employment under
-- a contract of service ascertained in accordance with section 37(1) of the Income Tax Act 1947".
-- Reg 2A(1): "Pursuant to section 8A(9) of the Act, sections 9A and 9B of the Act do not apply to any platform remuneration paid or
-- payable to a platform worker on or after 1 January 2025." (2): "In these Regulations, except in regulation 7A(4) and (4A),
-- 'income' excludes any platform remuneration paid or payable to a platform worker on or after 1 January 2025."
-- [S 888/2025 wef 01/01/2026 -- the date named is 1 January 2025, a year before the amendment took effect.]
GIVEN `assessable trade income` IS A NUMBER, `of which platform remuneration paid on or after 1 January 2025` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income under regulation 2A(2)` `assessable trade income` `of which platform remuneration paid on or after 1 January 2025` MEANS
    IF `of which platform remuneration paid on or after 1 January 2025` AT LEAST `assessable trade income` THEN 0
    ELSE `assessable trade income` MINUS `of which platform remuneration paid on or after 1 January 2025`

-- Reg 3(1): "Subject to paragraph (2), these Regulations apply to a self-employed person whose income is more than $6,000 for any
-- relevant year." (Paragraph (2), Members of Parliament, is not encoded.)
GIVEN `citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN, income IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Regulations apply under regulation 3(1)` IF
        `citizen or permanent resident`
    AND income GREATER THAN 6000

§§ `First Schedule item 23 -- the age columns`

-- The columns go by age "on 1 January of the relevant year": (2) "has not attained 35 years of age"; (3) "has attained 35 years of
-- age but has not attained 45"; (4) "has attained 45 ... but has not attained 50"; (5) "has attained 50".
-- Act s 2(1A)(a): "an individual attains a particular age expressed in years on the corresponding anniversary of the date of that
-- individual's birth". So on 1 January of year Y a person born in year B has attained Y - B if born on 1 January, else Y - B - 1.
-- (The 29 February rule in s 2(1A)(b) and reg 2(2) cannot bite on 1 January.)
GIVEN `relevant year` IS A NUMBER, `year of birth` IS A NUMBER, `born on 1 January` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the age attained on 1 January of the relevant year` `relevant year` `year of birth` `born on 1 January` MEANS
    IF `born on 1 January` THEN `relevant year` MINUS `year of birth`
    ELSE `relevant year` MINUS `year of birth` MINUS 1

-- Item 23: "For the relevant year beginning 1 January 2026 and every subsequent year, the contributions payable by a self-employed
-- person are as follows":
--   income not exceeding $6,000:                  Nil in every column;
--   exceeding $6,000, not exceeding $12,000:      4% / 4.5% / 5% / 5.25% "of the income ... for that year";
--   exceeding $12,000, not exceeding $18,000:     "the sum of $480 and 0.16 of the difference between the income ... for that year
--                                                 and $12,000" / $540 and 0.18 / $600 and 0.20 / $630 and 0.21;
--   exceeding $18,000:                            8% / 9% / 10% / 10.5% "of the income ... for that year, subject to a maximum of"
--                                                 $7,680 / $8,640 / $9,600 / $10,080.
-- ("less any allowance or honorarium he or she received for that year as a Member of Parliament" is dropped: MPs not encoded.)
-- NOTE: the 8% is on the WHOLE income, not on the income above $6,000; the middle band phases in from 4% to 8%.
DECLARE `Item 23 column` HAS
    `lower-band rate` IS A NUMBER
    `middle-band base` IS A NUMBER
    `middle-band factor` IS A NUMBER
    `top-band rate` IS A NUMBER
    `top-band maximum` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Item 23 column`
`the item 23 column for` age MEANS
    IF age LESS THAN 35 THEN `Item 23 column` WITH `lower-band rate` IS 0.04, `middle-band base` IS 480, `middle-band factor` IS 0.16, `top-band rate` IS 0.08, `top-band maximum` IS 7680
    ELSE IF age LESS THAN 45 THEN `Item 23 column` WITH `lower-band rate` IS 0.045, `middle-band base` IS 540, `middle-band factor` IS 0.18, `top-band rate` IS 0.09, `top-band maximum` IS 8640
         ELSE IF age LESS THAN 50 THEN `Item 23 column` WITH `lower-band rate` IS 0.05, `middle-band base` IS 600, `middle-band factor` IS 0.2, `top-band rate` IS 0.1, `top-band maximum` IS 9600
              ELSE `Item 23 column` WITH `lower-band rate` IS 0.0525, `middle-band base` IS 630, `middle-band factor` IS 0.21, `top-band rate` IS 0.105, `top-band maximum` IS 10080

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, income IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the item 23 amount before rounding` age income MEANS
    IF income AT MOST 6000 THEN 0
    ELSE IF income AT MOST 12000 THEN income TIMES c's `lower-band rate`
         ELSE IF income AT MOST 18000 THEN c's `middle-band base` PLUS c's `middle-band factor` TIMES (income MINUS 12000)
              ELSE IF income TIMES c's `top-band rate` GREATER THAN c's `top-band maximum` THEN c's `top-band maximum`
                   ELSE income TIMES c's `top-band rate`
    WHERE
        c MEANS `the item 23 column for` age

§§ `Regs 4(1)(m), 14 -- the amount`

-- Reg 4(1): "every self-employed person to whom these Regulations apply must pay contributions into the Fund on his or her own
-- behalf -- ... (m) at the applicable rate specified in the second, third, fourth and fifth columns of item 23 in the First Schedule
-- in respect of the relevant year beginning 1 January 2026 and every subsequent relevant year."
-- Reg 14: "In calculating the amount of contributions payable under regulation 4, 7, 7A, 8 or 8A, any fraction of a dollar is to be
-- disregarded."
GIVEN age IS A NUMBER, income IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the regulation 4 contribution` age income MEANS
    FLOOR (`the item 23 amount before rounding` age income)

§§ `Reg 8A -- estimated contributions deducted`

-- Reg 8A(1): the amount computed under reg 4(1) "(C) is to be reduced by the total amount of estimated contributions payable to the
-- Fund under section 9B of the Act for the self-employed person for the relevant year (E) (if any)." (2): "If E is more than C, the
-- contribution payable by the self-employed person under section 9A of the Act for that relevant year is nil."
GIVEN C IS A NUMBER, E IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution after regulation 8A` C E MEANS
    IF E AT LEAST C THEN 0 ELSE FLOOR (C MINUS E)

§§ `Reg 7A(4A) -- a self-employed person who is also a platform worker`

-- Reg 7A(4A): "where a self-employed person is during the relevant year also paid platform remuneration as a platform worker, the
-- contributions notice must state the amount of the contributions ... (a) as computed on the basis of the self-employed person's
-- income for the relevant year stated in a notice of assessment, less his or her total APE for each of the relevant months in that
-- year". APE is defined by reference to Fourth Schedule para 1 of the Act; it is an input here.
GIVEN `income stated in the notice of assessment` IS A NUMBER, `total APE for the relevant months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the income basis under regulation 7A(4A)` `income stated in the notice of assessment` `total APE for the relevant months` MEANS
    IF `total APE for the relevant months` AT LEAST `income stated in the notice of assessment` THEN 0
    ELSE `income stated in the notice of assessment` MINUS `total APE for the relevant months`

§§ `Reg 7A(2), (3) -- by when, and in instalments`

-- Reg 7A(2): "A self-employed person must pay the contributions for each relevant year not later than -- (a) 30 days after the date
-- of issue of the notice of computation or contributions notice (as the case may be) for the relevant year; or (b) where the Board
-- specifies an extended period of payment for the contributions for a relevant year -- the end of that extended period."
-- The date of issue is the Board's act and is an input; days are counted from it. INFERENCE (labelled): an "extended" period is
-- taken to be one ending more than 30 days after issue; 0 means none was specified.
GIVEN `the Board's extended period in days after issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day for paying under regulation 7A(2), in days after the notice` `the Board's extended period in days after issue` MEANS
    IF `the Board's extended period in days after issue` GREATER THAN 30 THEN `the Board's extended period in days after issue`
    ELSE 30

GIVEN `paid, in days after the notice was issued` IS A NUMBER, `the Board's extended period in days after issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid in time under regulation 7A(2)` IF
    `paid, in days after the notice was issued` AT MOST `the last day for paying under regulation 7A(2), in days after the notice` `the Board's extended period in days after issue`

-- Reg 7A(3): "The contributions for a relevant year may be paid in instalments, so long as the total amount of those contributions is
-- paid not later than the time of payment applicable to those contributions under paragraph (2)."
GIVEN `total paid by the last day` IS A NUMBER, `contributions payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instalments discharge the contributions under regulation 7A(3)` IF
    `total paid by the last day` AT LEAST `contributions payable`

-- Reg 16: contributions "must be paid within the time provided for in these Regulations despite any objection or appeal against the
-- notice of assessment unless the Board extends the time".
GIVEN `objection or appeal pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Board extends the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the time for paying is postponed` IF
    `the Board extends the time`

§§ `Regs 8, 13 -- additional contributions after recomputation`

-- Reg 8(1): where the contributions "recomputed in accordance with regulation 6, 7(6) or 7A(5) exceed the contributions already paid
-- ... the self-employed person must make such amount of additional contributions as is equivalent to the difference". (2): within
-- 30 days, or extended time, after the date of issue of the notice. Reg 13: "where the amount of additional contributions payable
-- for any relevant year -- (a) is less than one dollar, it is to be disregarded". Reg 14 disregards fractions of a dollar.
GIVEN recomputed IS A NUMBER, `already paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the additional contributions under regulation 8` recomputed `already paid` MEANS
    IF recomputed MINUS `already paid` LESS THAN 1 THEN 0
    ELSE FLOOR (recomputed MINUS `already paid`)

§§ `Reg 9A, Third Schedule -- the application to reduce`

-- Reg 9A(1): applies to a self-employed person "who during a relevant year starting on or after 1 January 2025 is also an employee,
-- a platform worker or both, and where contributions in respect of his or her wages or platform remuneration or both ... have been
-- made to the Board". (2): he "may apply in writing to the Board to reduce the amount of contributions he or she is liable to pay
-- ... so that the aggregate amount of all contributions paid into the self-employed person's account in the Fund (excluding any
-- contributions paid in respect of additional wages) for the relevant year does not exceed the maximum amount prescribed in the
-- Third Schedule."
-- Third Schedule: item 1 (relevant year starting 1 January 2025): below 35 $7,104; 35 to below 45 $7,992; 45 to below 50 $8,880;
-- 50 or older $9,324 (age on 1 January 2025). Item 2 (starting on or after 1 January 2026): $7,680 / $8,640 / $9,600 / $10,080 (age
-- on 1 January of the relevant year).
GIVEN `relevant year` IS A NUMBER, age IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Third Schedule maximum` `relevant year` age MEANS
    IF `relevant year` LESS THAN 2025 THEN 0
    ELSE IF `relevant year` EQUALS 2025 THEN
             IF age LESS THAN 35 THEN 7104
             ELSE IF age LESS THAN 45 THEN 7992
                  ELSE IF age LESS THAN 50 THEN 8880
                       ELSE 9324
         ELSE IF age LESS THAN 35 THEN 7680
              ELSE IF age LESS THAN 45 THEN 8640
                   ELSE IF age LESS THAN 50 THEN 9600
                        ELSE 10080

-- INFERENCE (labelled): "all contributions paid into the self-employed person's account" is read literally, and which of the
-- employment and platform contributions count is an input (the Board's figure). The reduction is the most that keeps the aggregate
-- at or under the maximum; reg 9A does not let it go below nil.
GIVEN `liable to pay` IS A NUMBER, `other contributions counted for the year` IS A NUMBER, `the maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution after a regulation 9A reduction` `liable to pay` `other contributions counted for the year` `the maximum` MEANS
    IF `other contributions counted for the year` AT LEAST `the maximum` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `liable to pay` PLUS `other contributions counted for the year` AT MOST `the maximum` THEN `liable to pay`
         ELSE `the maximum` MINUS `other contributions counted for the year`
